      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "PAUL D. CLEMENT, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument first this morning in No. 09-1227, Bond v. United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The standing of Petitioner to challenge the constitutionality of the Federal statute under which her liberty is being deprived should not be open to serious question. She clearly satisfies this Court's modern tripartite test for standing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Do our -- any of our opinions talk about the standing of the defendant? I can't think of one at the moment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Suppose I raise an Establishment Clause objection in a matter that -- that does not involve legislation and which our recent opinions say therefore does not violate the Establishment Clause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: So you want us to say that when there is a specific injury, specific to your client, that your client has the right to make any argument to show that the government has exceeded its powers under the Constitution, because those powers are limited to protect the liberties of the individual?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Can't there be some Tenth Amendment claims that go just to State prerogatives and not to the rights of individuals? Let's say there's a Federal statute that purports to regulate where a State locates its capital, or the -- the contents of a State flag, something like that. Wouldn't that go just to State prerogatives and not to individual rights?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Clement, if you are not making a commandeering claim, then we would be going out of our way to decide that question. And so, you know, are you making a commandeering claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Does that depend on the nature of the chemical that's involved? Suppose the chemical was -- was something that people would normally understand as the kind of chemical that would be used in a chemical weapon? Let's say it's Sarin does it matter that this case doesn't involve something like that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0000-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What do you say about the one thing -- the strongest point against you, I think, is a single sentence in that TVA case. It's only one sentence, but it's there in the opinion, and I think what it's saying, Justice Roberts says, well, he already finished, he just finished saying nobody -- Congress hasn't violated some rule against creating a system of regulation in this statute because it isn't regulation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0000-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Third Circuit erred in holding to the contrary. Now, the Third Circuit in reaching the contrary conclusion relied on this Court's decision in Tennessee Electric v. TVA, and we think that the court of appeals misread that case in concluding that it barred standing, not because it lacks a holding that does bar standing of certain types of claims that allege an invasion of State sovereignty, but because the kind of claim that Petitioner is making is not a Tenth Amendment reserved rights claim, but instead an enumerated powers claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, what if they argue -\u00ad what if she argues on remand, if there is a remand, that, assuming for the sake of argument Congress can enact any law that is necessary and proper to implement a treaty? The Tenth Amendment prohibits certain laws that intrude too heavily on State law enforcement prerogatives, State police power. If she makes that argument, which category does that fall into?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If this case does go back down to the Third Circuit, a petitioner can make the argument that this law exceeds the enumerated powers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner said the Tenth Amendment argument raised by Bond was not critical to Bond's other constitutional challenges. It is ancillary to Bond's main argument that Congress acted outside of its enumerated powers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Stephen R. McAllister",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF STEPHEN R. McALLISTER, AS AMICUS CURIAE, IN SUPPORT OF JUDGEMENT BELOW"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Excuse me. What do you see specifically? Because there's a lot of discussion about labels and what the labels mean in this case. But tell me specifically what -- not the word she uses, but the specific ways in which prudential considerations bar her standing; meaning: What about the nature of her claim prudentially should counsel us against giving her standing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McAllister",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McALLISTER: Well, I would say at least a couple things, Your Honor. One is, the usual rule of prudential third-party standing considers the alignment or lack of alignment between the interests of the third party making the claim and the party who is not present whose claim it really is. And in this case, there's really no argument that her interests align with those of the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. The Commonwealth in fact prosecuted her and it did not stop her. It was unsuccessful as a deterrent. And later, when local police wouldn't be involved, the Federal Government got involved."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Do you think Pennsylvania would be upset that the Federal Government got her when they couldn't?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McAllister",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McALLISTER: No, that's my point. And so my point is that her interests are directly contrary to Pennsylvania's interests. So she's not stepping in saying: I share the interests of the State; therefore, let me articulate and argue the interests of the State."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: That's what she's trying to do. Why doesn't she have standing to make that argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McAllister",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0002-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McALLISTER: Because the lower courts, at least, in their defense, understood this to be a Tenth Amendment claim, and there are reasons for that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If I'm right, what's comparable to that in this case? Is there some claim that she's making that it would be constitutional if they agreed in the State and it wouldn't be if not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could you just articulate for me -- we're speaking in generalities -\u00ad what in the nature of her claim, taking the labels away, do you think is a pure Tenth Amendment challenge?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McAllister",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McALLISTER: As I understand her complaint, basically her argument is that unless this statute is authorized by something in Article I, section 8, the first 17 clauses, there's no power to enact it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul D. Clement",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. Just a few points in rebuttal. First of all, one reason not to carve out a special rule for commandeering claims is that not all commandeering claims are created equal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
      "evidence_id": "ev-43a54698a222-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Plain error should be a two-way street, and they should not be allowed to sneak the Commerce Clause back into the case at this late stage."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1227",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "43a54698a222bb57dc0df421042515690658977ca55b10bc127b152cbf0aecad",
